Documentation of the entire inference process. A "complete reasoning trace" refers explicitly to a comprehensive, self-contained audit trail capturing every aspect of how and why an inference or decision was reached, in a fully reconstructible manner. This complete trace enables precise auditing, compliance verification, debugging, and in-depth analysis, preserving transparency, accountability, and trustworthiness of the inference process. For instance, a healthcare diagnostic system would generate a complete reasoning trace documenting exactly what patient data triggered specific diagnostic rules, what logic was applied, which research publications informed conclusions, and how each intermediate step contributed to the final diagnostic recommendation, providing an auditable justification for medical decisions."
